csk_saas.db-journal
# ronin workspace config. Default-deny with an explicit allowlist, because the
# directory holds both plaintext API keys (config.toml) and the four files a team
# is *supposed* to share. The old blanket `.ronin/` ignored all of it — and since
# git does not descend into an ignored directory, no negation inside could rescue
# anything — so the committed project settings, subagents, slash commands and MCP
# server list were silently untrackable.
#
# `.ronin/*` (not `.ronin/`) matches only direct children and lets git descend, so
# the negations below work. Anything not named here stays ignored: a new file some
# code drops in this directory is secret until someone decides otherwise.
.ronin/*
!.ronin/settings.json
!.ronin/mcp.json
!.ronin/hooks.json
!.ronin/agents/
!.ronin/commands/
# ...but never the local layer, even though its parent is now walkable.
.ronin/settings.local.json
.ronin/*.local.json
# legacy (pre-rename) — still ignored for older checkouts.
# NB: git does not support trailing comments on pattern lines.
.csk/
# generated media (images / videos) dropped in the repo root
ronin_image_*.png
ronin_image_*.jpg
ronin_video_*.mp4
